5 #edb/ref 17592186415449 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415452 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415456 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415457 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415464 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1077 "selection" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415464 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415473 1079 #uuid "e80361a1-690f-54bf-a979-055f8bec64f8" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415448 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415453 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415454 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415459 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415463 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1077 "selection" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415463 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415474 1079 #uuid "f920ea7f-06a7-52e9-8586-d0e6b44af6b3" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415475 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415470 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415475 1069 "q-140048" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415475 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415475 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415475 1072 #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415475 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415476 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415471 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415476 1069 "q-42469" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415476 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415476 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415476 1072 #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415476 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415477 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415472 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415477 1069 "q-42464" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415477 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415477 1071 "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415477 1072 #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415477 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415474 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415478 1069 "q-42881" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415478 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415478 1071 "Find $3det(A)-det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415478 1072 #uuid "e897ce2c-45dd-5cf3-9d25-ca84c0dd6ea8" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415478 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-det(B)=3\\cdot 6-0=18.$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415479 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415473 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415479 1069 "q-43307" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415479 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415479 1071 "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has two proportional rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415479 1072 #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415479 1074 "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415480 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415484 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415480 1062 #uuid "0922e6fb-1dc5-5a88-a985-bdf2643cb465" 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415480 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415477 13194139534238 17592186045417 true] [17592186415481 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415482 13194139